    "points": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "heading": "Simple tenses in context",
        "body": "Deepen only the simple set. Pick one regular verb and conjugate first-person singular in present, imperfect/past progressive, simple past, future, and conditional.\n\nWrite five minimal sentences, one per tense, changing the time frame (today / as a child / yesterday / tomorrow / if I could). Notice how imperfect does not close the action while simple past does.\n\nContrast past endings with progressive/used-to forms so you do not mix them when writing. Goal: five correct sentences without looking at a chart."
      }
    ],
